==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|her#Etymology_2_3}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hēr|t=at this place}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hēr}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hē₂r}}, from {{suffix|gem-pro|*hiz|*r|nocat=1}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro||*kís}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ḱe}} + {{m|ine-pro|*ís}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|stq|hier}}, {{cog|fy|hjir}}, {{cog|nl|hier}}, {{cog|nds-de|hier}}, {{cog|de|hier}}, {{cog|da|her}}, {{cog|sv|här}}, {{cog|no|her}}, {{cog|fo|her}}, {{cog|is|hér}}. Also related to the English pronoun {{m|en|he|t=this/that person}}, and the words {{m|en|hither|t=to this place}} and {{m|en|hence|t=from this place}}.
{{col-bottom}}

