===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|location}} In, on, or at this [[place]] (a place perceived to be close to the speaker); ''compare [[there]]''.
#: {{synonyms|en|right here|q1=emphatic}}
#: {{ux|en|You wait '''here''' while I fetch my coat.}}
#: {{ux|en|Ms. Doe is not '''here''' at the moment.}}
#: {{ux|en|It says '''here''' that he died in 1970.}}
#: {{ux|en|The air '''here''' is foul.}}
#: {{ux|en|The view up '''here''' is better than the view down there!}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Here''' is the report that you asked for.|q=''inverted use''}}
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Diet of Worms|'''Here''' I stand}}.}}
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Kilroy was here|Kilroy was '''here'''.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|canto=VII|text=Dark house, by which once more I stand / '''Here''' in the long unlovely street,}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=w:Omar Khadr|title=Affidavit of Omar Ahmed Khadr
|passage=The Canadian visitor stated, “I’m not '''here''' to help you. I’m not '''here''' to do anything for you. I’m just '''here''' to get information.”}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170918070146/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-3-i-am-here/3126527.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Oh, yes. I am '''here'''! &mdash; Good. You are there.
#*:: {{audio|en|Oh, yes. I am here.ogg|a=US}}
## {{lb|en|abstract}} At this point or stage (in a process, [[argument]], [[narration]], etc.)
##: {{ux|en|I've had enough of peeling potatoes. I'm stopping '''here'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''Here''' endeth the lesson.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1796|author=w:George Washington|title=s:Washington's Farewell Address
|passage='''Here''', perhaps I ought to stop.}}
##* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=6|passage=&ldquo;And drove away&mdash;away.&rdquo; Sophia broke down '''here'''. Even at this moment she was subconsciously comparing her rendering of the part of the forlorn bride with Miss Marie Lohr's.}}
## {{lb|en|abstract}} In this matter.
##: {{ux|en|You say that all men are born equal, but '''here''' I must disagree with you.}}
## {{lb|en|as complement of 'be'}} Notionally at the speaker's location by virtue of happening now.
##: {{ux|en|Flu season is '''here'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|Christmas will soon be '''here'''.}}
## {{lb|en|abstract}} In this [[context]].
##: {{ux|en|Derivatives can refer to anything that is derived from something else, but '''here''' they refer specifically to functions that give the slope of the tangent line to a curve.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1872|month=May|author=w:Edward Burnett Tylor|title=[[s:Popular Science Monthly/Volume 1/May 1872/Quetelet on the Science of Man|Quetelet on the Science of Man]]|journal=w:Popular Science Monthly|volume=1
|passage=The two great generalizations which the veteran Belgian astronomer has brought to bear on physiological and mental science, and which it is proposed to describe popularly '''here''', may be briefly defined:}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 15 1904|author=w:William James|title=The Chicago School|journal=w:Psychological Bulletin|section=1.1, pages 1-5
|passage=The briefest characterization is all that will be attempted '''here'''.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{n-g|After the name of a person perceived as located close to the speaker, used familiarly to indicate that person.}} 
##: {{ux|en|Jim '''here''' has been with the company for twenty years.}}
## {{lb|en|informal|or|dialect}} {{n-g|After certain determiners, especially 'this' and 'these', used to emphasise demonstrative sense; see also '''[[this here]]'''.}}
##: {{ux|en|This '''here''' orange is too sour.}}
##: {{ux|en|Both '''{{'}}ere''' buckets 'ave 'oles in 'em.}}
## [[alive|Alive]]
# {{lb|en|location}} To this [[place]]; {{n-g|used in place of the literary or archaic [[hither]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|Please come '''here'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1891|author=w:Charlotte Perkins Gilman|title=s:The Yellow Wall-Paper
|passage=He said we came '''here''' solely on my account, that I was to have perfect rest and all the air I could get.}}

